#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "1. Create an application"
msgstr "1. Create an application"

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "In the Developer Portal, choose New application and give it a name. The application comes with a bot account."
msgstr "In the Developer Portal, choose New application and give it a name. The application comes with a bot account."

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "Open My applications"
msgstr "Open My applications"

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "2. Copy the token"
msgstr "2. Copy the token"

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "Open the bot's settings and copy its token. Whoever has the token controls the bot."
msgstr "Open the bot's settings and copy its token. Whoever has the token controls the bot."

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "Keep the token in an environment variable or a secret store. Never put it in code, in a repository or in a screenshot. If it leaks, reset it at once."
msgstr "Keep the token in an environment variable or a secret store. Never put it in code, in a repository or in a screenshot. If it leaks, reset it at once."

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "3. Install the bot in a test server"
msgstr "3. Install the bot in a test server"

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "Open the OAuth2 tab of your application, choose the permissions the bot needs and open the install link. Pick a server where you have Manage Server."
msgstr "Open the OAuth2 tab of your application, choose the permissions the bot needs and open the install link. Pick a server where you have Manage Server."

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "4. Get the SDK"
msgstr "4. Get the SDK"

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "You need Node.js 22 or newer. The zrzur-bot SDK handles the gateway, commands and replies for you. You can also work without any library: the API is plain HTTP and WebSocket."
msgstr "You need Node.js 22 or newer. The zrzur-bot SDK handles the gateway, commands and replies for you. You can also work without any library: the API is plain HTTP and WebSocket."

#: src/interface/developers/docs/GettingStarted.tsx
msgid "About the SDKs"
